d":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi, I'm trying to bundle this file with rollup `0.34.1`\n\n_main.js_\n\n``` js\nimport { Something } from './lib'\n\nSomething();\n```\n\n_something.js_\n\n``` js\nexport function Something () {\n   // do some magic in the brower\n}\n```\n\n(Using an express middleware)\n\n``` js\nrollup.rollup({\n    entry: 'main.js',\n    plugins: [\n        babel(),\n        nodeResolve({\n            jsnext: true,\n            main: true,\n            preferBuiltins: true\n        }),\n        commonjs()\n    ],\n    treeshake: true\n})\n.then(bundle => bundle.generate({ format: 'iife' }))\n.then(result => {\n    res.status(200)\n    .type('application/javascript')\n    .send(result.code);\n})\n.catch(next);\n```\n\nThe output I get with **treeshake: true** is \n\n``` js\n(function () {\n    'use strict';\n\n\n\n}());\n```\n\nan empty IIFE.\n\nUsing **treeshake: false**\n\n``` js\n(function () {\n    'use strict';\n\n    function Something() {\n        // do some magic in the brower\n    }\n\n    Something();\n\n}());\n```\n\nI've also tried using a `moduleName` but it didn't help.\n\nAm I missing something? Is it normal that my main file gets shaken like that? Is there an option to disable tree shaking only on the main file and keep shaking all the imported libraries?\n","closed_by":{"login":"Rich-Harris","id":1162160,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjIxNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1162160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris","html_url":"https://github.com/Rich-Harris","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/use